            <div xml:id="d217-a6">

                <pb facs="0427" n="1387" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1387"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Articles</hi> 1 <hi rendition="#italic">and</hi> 2 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">of decree of October</hi> 21, 1880.</head>
                <list>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 1. The impost of damage is
                        established in the ultramarine Portuguese provinces, collected from national
                        and foreign navigation of long voyage or <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >cabotage</hi>, in the form prescribed in the following article.</item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. National or foreign sailing or
                        steam vessels which go into the ultramarine Portuguese ports are subject to
                        the tonnage tax fixed in the annexed table.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-10-21">October 21, 1880</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
